The International Olympic Committee (IOC) is seeking advanced insights into athlete performance, 
country-wise medal trends, and sport-specific dominance across Olympic Games. Using historical 
Olympic data, you are tasked with building analytical solutions that help track achievements, 
evaluate performance KPIs, and forecast future outcomes for strategic planning and athlete 
development.

📄 Page 1: Global Medal Overview
KPIs / Metrics:

Total Medals Awarded
Total Countries Participated
Top 10 Countries by Total Medals
Medal Trends Over the Years
Year-wise Total Events Held
 

📄 Page 2: Country Insights
KPIs / Metrics:

Total Athletes Represented
Total Medals Won
Medal Efficiency (Medals per 100 Athletes)
Medal Distribution (Gold, Silver, Bronze)
Year-wise Medal Count for Country
Best Performing Sports by Country
 

📄 Page 3: Athlete Spotlight
KPIs / Metrics:

Total Athletes
Top 10 Athletes by Total Medals
Medal-Winning Athletes vs Total Athletes
Most Participated Athletes (Olympic Appearances)
Athlete Age Distribution at Medal Wins
Gender Distribution of Medal Winners
 

📄 Page 4: Sport & Event Analysis
KPIs / Metrics:

Total Sports/Events
Events Added per Year
Top Sports by Medals Awarded
Country Dominance in Sports
Sport-wise Athlete Participation
Sport-wise Medal Trends Over Time
 

📄 Page 5: Host Country Analysis
KPIs / Metrics:

Total Olympics Hosted per Country
Medal Count as Host vs Non-Host
Host Country Medal Trend
Events Conducted in Host Olympics
 

📄 Page 6: Gender & Demographics
KPIs / Metrics:

Male vs Female Athlete Count Over Years
Gender-wise Medal Distribution
Youngest & Oldest Medal Winners
Avg. Age of Participants by Year
Participation by Age Group
